      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُهُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ طَافَ طَوَافَ اَلْحَجِّ وَ طَوَافَ اَلنِّسَاءِ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَسْعَى بَيْنَ اَلصَّفَا وَ اَلْمَرْوَةِ قَالَ «لاَ يَضُرُّهُ يَطُوفُ بَيْنَ اَلصَّفَا وَ اَلْمَرْوَةِ وَ قَدْ فَرَغَ مِنْ حَجِّهِ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2777 - Ishaq ibn Ammar narrated from Sama'ah ibn Mehran, from Imam Abu Al-Hasan Al-Madhi (as), who said: I asked him about a man who performed the Tawaf of Hajj and the Tawaf al-Nisa before performing the sa‘i between Safa and Marwa.\nImam (as) said: \"It does not harm him; he should perform the sa‘i between Safa and Marwa, and he has completed his Hajj.\""
        ]
      }
